{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1072: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. For any prime $p$, let $f(p)$ be the least integer such that $f(p)!+1\\equiv 0\\pmod{p}$.\n\nIs it true that there are infinitely many $p$ for which $f(p)=p-1$?\nIs it true that $f(p)/p\\to 0$ for almost all $p$? Current best: Questions formulated by Erd\\H{o}s, Hardy, and Subbarao \\cite{HaSu02}, who believed that the number of $p\\leq x$ for which $f(p)=p-1$ is $o(x/\\log x)$. Prize: no. OEIS: A072937, A073944, A154554. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_ae63813a370e5a6c1f499cc754638c4af5ee2187900c4b71e50fcb15501cf6a4","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1072","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_746f07a37008323a","object_root":"sha256:1e724fe51bc7af05f4cddd7e0c27c37012830e22a0ef72eaeedf87021c45b3be","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1072"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}